    "reason": "The user asserted a general legal precedence rule (final permit over fact sheet on conflict). Two plausible encodings were dry-run\u2014one as a world-level legal fact and one as a purpose-specific analysis policy\u2014and they produced identical measurable outcomes on this dataset: both added one document_kind_precedence row, both increased unresolved holes by one group and one instance (splitting other document-kind authority into permit_document_authority_other_kinds), and left all other hole counts unchanged. Because the interpretations did not diverge in consequence here, no clarification is required to choose between them; the world-level encoding matches the utterance's legal framing and the proposal's epistemic basis.",
